Emissions:
With all 1,000,000,000 minted into circulation at launch and the mint authority revoked, Seasons leverages a multitude of chronologically varying lockers to manage the $SEAS token supply.
Lockers, belonging to specific causes, periodically mature and release $SEAS back to their originating destinations; once matured, the state/degree of need for the $SEAS token at that moment in time (based on historic trails and near-term assumptions) is assessed, and in the event that the tokens are found to be of no critical service, they are once again relocked. However, if $SEAS tokens are determined to be an important tool, then only a necessary portion of tokens is retained and the remainder relocked.
As of 04/08/2026, supply is as follows:
Max Supply: 1,000,000,000 {100%}
Supply Policy: Fixed
Inflation: N/A
In Circulation: 333,000,000 {~33.3%}
Out Of Circulation: 667,000,000 {~66.7%}
Locked: ~600,300,00 {~60.03%}
Immobile: 66,700,000 {~6.67%}
Lock Periods are uniform for all allocations. Once unlocked, the project's state is assessed, and tokens are either relocked for the same duration or repurposed if certain quantitative criteria are met.
Functions: are not limited to the descriptions provided. While each address will adhere as tightly to its dedicated purpose as possible, the broad scope and nature of potential uses are beyond listing; thus, the reader is asked to allow for minor variance.
Fund Use: from any of the operational addresses shall be publicly recorded and communicated whenever the use happens.
Wallet Authority: assigned wallets will remain the authorities over their allocated supplies. In the event a new wallet authority is required, one shall be assigned and publicly registered.

Seasons Decentralized Autonomous Organization
NOT YET OPERATIONAL
The DAO element of SEASONS shall be instantiated only after certain qualitative and quantitative achievements are acquired.
Any material provided here is for general ideation purposes; it does not reflect the final implementation choice.
NOT YET OPERATIONAL
Decentralization must be achieved progressively; thus, as Seasons matures, DAO components shall be steadily injected into the system's processes, one at a time.
Tentatively earmarked for development in H2 of 2027, this aspect of the project shall be regularly revisited for adaptation.
NOT YET OPERATIONAL
Purpose
The Seasons DAO serves as a community form for network members who possess notable impact/weight to coordinate and collaborate. It is a communication platform dedicated to the Yield 3.0 mechanism, where the system's power users make product-defining decisions.
Ultimately, the DAO inherits control over the yield mechanism, becoming the steward and guardian of the yield 3.0 system.
Functionality
The DAO shall be able to submit, vote on, and discuss SEAips (Season Improvement Proposals) as they pertain to the mechanical configuration of the Seasons Yield System. Enabling users to direct the flows of capital, alter distribution frequencies, calibrate fees, and then experience the outcome of their decision-making, unlocks a deeper bond and, in turn, alignment between users and the Yield 3.0 mechanism's well-being.
The DAO will have autonomy over every individual element of each module within the Seasons Yield system; allowing the members to intimately influence how the system works. A shorthand list of examples is as follows:
- Enable “asset nomination” {community selected inclusion sets}
- Enable “delisting requests” {community selected inclusion sets}
- Enable “TTT Fee range” {adjustment of fee size}
- Enable “TTT Fee gauge” {adjustment of fee allocation}
- Enable “SSYM Fee range” {adjustment of fee size}
- Enable “SSYM Fee gauge” {adjustment of fee allocation}
- Enable “Distribution triggers” {adjustment of when/how assets are distributed}
- Enable “Inclusion Set Refinements” (adjustment of proportions & number of assets included)
- Enable “Node Inclusion List" {expand or contract accessiblity}
- Enable “YMS behavior" {strategic acquisition/distribution schemes)
- et al.

